<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Sultanate of Moheli</h1><p class="st-meta">1830 CE – 1909 CE (approx.) · capital Fomboni</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The smallest Comoran sultanate, founded by a Merina prince and ruled by Queen Djoumbe Fatima before falling under France.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1830 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramanetaka">Ramanetaka</a>, a Merina prince and governor who had fled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>, seized control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moheli">Moheli</a> (Mwali) and set himself up as sultan with the Muslim name Abderremane, displacing the island's earlier rulers.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramanetaka">Ramanetaka's</a> death in 1842 his young daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/djoumbe-fatima">Djoumbe Fatima</a> became queen. Her long reign saw rival French and British influence and a controversial plantation lease to a French trader, while the small island lived from fishing, farming and trade with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sultanate-of-zanzibar">Zanzibar</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> culture shaped court life at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fomboni">Fomboni</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> imposed a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> in 1886, and the last queen, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salima-machamba">Salima Machamba</a>, abdicated before the island was annexed and attached to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-mayotte-and-dependencies">Colony of Mayotte and Dependencies</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moheli">Moheli</a> is now part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comoro-islands">Union of the Comoros</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="sultanate, 1830 CE – 1909 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">sultanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:96.12%;width:1.57%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1830 CE – 1909 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Fomboni</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ramanetaka, Djoumbe Fatima, Salima Machamba</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Comorian (Shimwali)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/comoros">Comoros</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mwali, Moili</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1870&amp;focus=sultanate-of-moheli" aria-label="Sultanate of Moheli on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5882 2635 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sultanate of Moheli lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6202 2891L6286 3134M6202 2891L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6286 3134h0M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6202 2891h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6202 2891h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Fomboni. <a href="/atlas?year=1870&amp;focus=sultanate-of-moheli">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
